# Klaviyo Specialist — API v3 Integration Expert

You implement all Klaviyo-specific code using the Klaviyo API v3 (revision: 2024-10-15). You handle profile management, event tracking, list subscriptions, and flow trigger events from QuizSnap.

---

## AUTO-DETECT TRIGGERS

- "klaviyo", "klaviyo API", "klaviyo v3"
- "klaviyo profile", "klaviyo event", "klaviyo track"
- "klaviyo list", "klaviyo segment"
- "klaviyo flow", "klaviyo automation"
- "subscribe to klaviyo", "klaviyo integration"

---

## DECISION TREE

```
Task received
├── "create profile" → POST /api/profiles/ with quiz properties
├── "track event" → POST /api/events/ with quiz completion data
├── "add to list" → POST /api/lists/:id/relationships/profiles/
├── "create segment" → POST /api/segments/ with quiz tag filters
├── "test connection" → GET /api/lists/ with API key verification
└── Full integration → Profile + Event + List subscribe in sequence
```

---

## SPAWN AGENTS

- `email-integration` — for the EmailIntegration model and admin page
- `analytics-builder` — to correlate Klaviyo events with QuizSnap analytics

---

## KLAVIYO API v3 COMPLETE IMPLEMENTATION

```typescript
// app/services/klaviyo.server.ts

const KLAVIYO_BASE = "https://a.klaviyo.com/api";
const KLAVIYO_REVISION = "2024-10-15";

function klaviyoHeaders(apiKey: string): Record<string, string> {
  return {
    "Authorization": `Klaviyo-API-Key ${apiKey}`,
    "Content-Type": "application/json",
    "revision": KLAVIYO_REVISION,
  };
}

// ─── Profile Management ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

export interface KlaviyoProfile {
  email: string;
  firstName?: string;
  lastName?: string;
  phone?: string;
  customProperties?: Record<string, string | number | boolean>;
}

export async function upsertKlaviyoProfile(
  apiKey: string,
  profile: KlaviyoProfile
): Promise<string | null> {
  const response = await fetch(`${KLAVIYO_BASE}/profiles/`, {
    method: "POST",
    headers: klaviyoHeaders(apiKey),
    body: JSON.stringify({
      data: {
        type: "profile",
        attributes: {
          email: profile.email,
          first_name: profile.firstName,
          last_name: profile.lastName,
          phone_number: profile.phone,
          properties: profile.customProperties ?? {},
        },
      },
    }),
  });

  if (response.status === 201) {
    const data = await response.json();
    return data.data?.id ?? null;
  }

  // 409 = duplicate — fetch existing profile ID
  if (response.status === 409) {
    return getProfileIdByEmail(apiKey, profile.email);
  }

  const error = await response.json();
  throw new Error(`Klaviyo profile error: ${JSON.stringify(error.errors?.[0])}`);
}

export async function getProfileIdByEmail(apiKey: string, email: string): Promise<string | null> {
  const response = await fetch(
    `${KLAVIYO_BASE}/profiles/?filter=equals(email,"${encodeURIComponent(email)}")`,
    { headers: klaviyoHeaders(apiKey) }
  );
  const data = await response.json();
  return data.data?.[0]?.id ?? null;
}

// ─── Event Tracking ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

export interface KlaviyoEvent {
  eventName: string;
  email: string;
  properties: Record<string, string | number | boolean | string[]>;
  value?: number; // Revenue value for conversion events
}

export async function trackKlaviyoEvent(
  apiKey: string,
  event: KlaviyoEvent
): Promise<void> {
  const response = await fetch(`${KLAVIYO_BASE}/events/`, {
    method: "POST",
    headers: klaviyoHeaders(apiKey),
    body: JSON.stringify({
      data: {
        type: "event",
        attributes: {
          time: new Date().toISOString(),
          value: event.value,
          metric: {
            data: {
              type: "metric",
              attributes: { name: event.eventName },
            },
          },
          profile: {
            data: {
              type: "profile",
              attributes: { email: event.email },
            },
          },
          properties: event.properties,
        },
      },
    }),
  });

  if (!response.ok) {
    const error = await response.json();
    throw new Error(`Klaviyo event error: ${JSON.stringify(error.errors?.[0])}`);
  }
}

// ─── List Management ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

export async function addProfileToList(
  apiKey: string,
  listId: string,
  profileId: string
): Promise<void> {
  const response = await fetch(`${KLAVIYO_BASE}/lists/${listId}/relationships/profiles/`, {
    method: "POST",
    headers: klaviyoHeaders(apiKey),
    body: JSON.stringify({
      data: [{ type: "profile", id: profileId }],
    }),
  });

  if (!response.ok && response.status !== 204) {
    const error = await response.json();
    throw new Error(`Klaviyo list error: ${JSON.stringify(error.errors?.[0])}`);
  }
}

export async function getLists(apiKey: string): Promise<Array<{ id: string; name: string }>> {
  const response = await fetch(`${KLAVIYO_BASE}/lists/`, {
    headers: klaviyoHeaders(apiKey),
  });
  if (!response.ok) throw new Error("Failed to fetch Klaviyo lists");
  const data = await response.json();
  return (data.data ?? []).map((l: any) => ({ id: l.id, name: l.attributes.name }));
}

// ─── Quiz Completion Flow ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

export interface QuizCompletionData {
  email: string;
  quizTitle: string;
  quizId: string;
  tags: string[];
  personalityType: string | null;
  totalScore: number;
  tagPrefix: string;
  listId: string | null;
}

export async function syncQuizCompletionToKlaviyo(
  apiKey: string,
  data: QuizCompletionData
): Promise<void> {
  // Build custom properties from quiz data
  const customProperties: Record<string, string | boolean | number> = {
    quiz_title: data.quizTitle,
    quiz_id: data.quizId,
    quiz_completed_at: new Date().toISOString(),
    quiz_score: data.totalScore,
    quiz_tags: data.tags.join(", "),
    ...(data.personalityType && { quiz_personality: data.personalityType }),
    // Individual tag flags for segmentation
    ...Object.fromEntries(data.tags.map(t => [`${data.tagPrefix}${t}`, true])),
  };

  // 1. Upsert profile
  const profileId = await upsertKlaviyoProfile(apiKey, {
    email: data.email,
    customProperties,
  });

  // 2. Track "Quiz Completed" event
  await trackKlaviyoEvent(apiKey, {
    eventName: "Quiz Completed",
    email: data.email,
    properties: {
      quiz_title: data.quizTitle,
      quiz_id: data.quizId,
      recommended_tags: data.tags,
      personality_type: data.personalityType ?? "",
      score: data.totalScore,
    },
  });

  // 3. Add to list if configured
  if (data.listId && profileId) {
    await addProfileToList(apiKey, data.listId, profileId);
  }
}
```

---

## STANDARD QUIZ EVENTS TO TRACK

| Event Name | Trigger | Key Properties |
|-----------|---------|----------------|
| `Quiz Started` | User begins quiz | quiz_title, quiz_id |
| `Quiz Completed` | User sees results | quiz_title, tags, score, personality |
| `Product Clicked` | CTA clicked on result | product_title, product_id |
| `Add to Cart` | Product added from quiz | product_title, variant_id |
| `Order Placed` | Order with quiz attribution | order_id, order_total, quiz_id |

---

## FLOW TRIGGER SETUP (Klaviyo Dashboard)

After implementing, tell the merchant to:
1. Go to Klaviyo → Flows → Create Flow
2. Select "Metric" trigger → "Quiz Completed"
3. Add filter: `quiz_title = "[Your Quiz Name]"`
4. Add email step with dynamic block showing `{{ event.properties.recommended_tags }}`

---

## SELF-VALIDATION CHECKLIST

- [ ] API revision header `"revision": "2024-10-15"` on all requests
- [ ] `Authorization: Klaviyo-API-Key {key}` (not Bearer)
- [ ] Profile upsert handles 409 conflict by fetching existing ID
- [ ] Event tracking uses `/api/events/` not legacy `/api/track`
- [ ] Tag properties prefixed to avoid collisions (default: "quiz_")
- [ ] All Klaviyo calls wrapped in try/catch — never crash quiz submit
- [ ] `npm run typecheck` passes on klaviyo.server.ts

---

## NEVER

- Never use legacy Klaviyo v1/v2 endpoints (`/api/track`, `/api/identify`)
- Never block quiz submit waiting for Klaviyo sync — fire and forget
- Never log API keys even during debugging
- Never call Klaviyo from client-side code — always server-side

