# Klaviyo Specialist — API v3 Integration

## AUTO-DETECT TRIGGERS
- User mentions: klaviyo, klaviyo api, klaviyo event, klaviyo profile, klaviyo list
- Quiz completion needs to fire Klaviyo tracking event
- Email capture should add customer to Klaviyo list
- Klaviyo flow automation triggered by quiz events

## DECISION TREE
```
Klaviyo needed? →
  Track event? → POST /api/events (profile + event in one call)
  Add to list? → POST /api/profile-subscription-bulk-create-jobs
  Update profile? → POST /api/profiles (upsert)
  Get list ID? → GET /api/lists (for settings UI)
  API key valid? → GET /api/lists with key, check 200 vs 401
  Error? → Log and continue (non-blocking, never fail quiz)
```

## KLAVIYO API CLIENT (No SDK — Direct Fetch)

```typescript
// app/utils/klaviyo.server.ts
const KLAVIYO_API_VERSION = "2024-02-15";
const KLAVIYO_BASE = "https://a.klaviyo.com/api";

interface KlaviyoRequestOptions {
  method?: "GET" | "POST" | "PATCH" | "DELETE";
  body?: unknown;
}

async function klaviyoRequest(
  apiKey: string,
  endpoint: string,
  options: KlaviyoRequestOptions = {}
): Promise<{ ok: boolean; status: number; data?: unknown; error?: string }> {
  try {
    const resp = await fetch(`${KLAVIYO_BASE}/${endpoint}`, {
      method: options.method ?? "GET",
      headers: {
        "Authorization": `Klaviyo-API-Key ${apiKey}`,
        "Content-Type": "application/json",
        "revision": KLAVIYO_API_VERSION,
        "Accept": "application/json",
      },
      body: options.body ? JSON.stringify(options.body) : undefined,
    });

    if (resp.status === 204) return { ok: true, status: 204 };

    const data = await resp.json();
    if (!resp.ok) {
      const message = data.errors?.[0]?.detail ?? `Klaviyo error ${resp.status}`;
      return { ok: false, status: resp.status, error: message };
    }

    return { ok: true, status: resp.status, data };
  } catch (err) {
    return { ok: false, status: 0, error: "Network error reaching Klaviyo" };
  }
}

export async function validateKlaviyoApiKey(apiKey: string): Promise<boolean> {
  const result = await klaviyoRequest(apiKey, "lists?page[size]=1");
  return result.ok;
}
```

## TRACK QUIZ COMPLETION EVENT

```typescript
// app/utils/klaviyo.server.ts (continued)

interface QuizCompletionEventData {
  email: string;
  firstName?: string;
  lastName?: string;
  quizTitle: string;
  quizId: string;
  resultPageTitle: string;
  score: number;
  recommendedProducts: Array<{ title: string; url: string; imageUrl?: string; price: string }>;
  emailCaptured: boolean;
  completedAt: string;
}

export async function trackQuizCompletion(
  apiKey: string,
  data: QuizCompletionEventData
): Promise<{ success: boolean; error?: string }> {
  const result = await klaviyoRequest(apiKey, "events", {
    method: "POST",
    body: {
      data: {
        type: "event",
        attributes: {
          properties: {
            quiz_id: data.quizId,
            quiz_title: data.quizTitle,
            result_page: data.resultPageTitle,
            quiz_score: data.score,
            email_captured: data.emailCaptured,
            top_product: data.recommendedProducts[0]?.title ?? null,
            recommended_products: data.recommendedProducts.map(p => ({
              title: p.title,
              url: p.url,
              image: p.imageUrl,
              price: p.price,
            })),
            recommended_count: data.recommendedProducts.length,
            completed_at: data.completedAt,
          },
          metric: {
            data: {
              type: "metric",
              attributes: { name: "Quiz Completed" }
            }
          },
          profile: {
            data: {
              type: "profile",
              attributes: {
                email: data.email,
                first_name: data.firstName ?? null,
                last_name: data.lastName ?? null,
                properties: {
                  last_quiz_result: data.resultPageTitle,
                  last_quiz_score: data.score,
                  last_quiz_title: data.quizTitle,
                  last_quiz_completed: data.completedAt,
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  });

  if (!result.ok) {
    console.error("Klaviyo event tracking failed:", result.error);
    return { success: false, error: result.error };
  }

  return { success: true };
}
```

## LIST SUBSCRIPTION

```typescript
export async function subscribeToKlaviyoList(
  apiKey: string,
  listId: string,
  profile: {
    email: string;
    firstName?: string;
    lastName?: string;
    phone?: string;
  }
): Promise<{ success: boolean; error?: string }> {
  const result = await klaviyoRequest(
    apiKey,
    "profile-subscription-bulk-create-jobs",
    {
      method: "POST",
      body: {
        data: {
          type: "profile-subscription-bulk-create-job",
          attributes: {
            profiles: {
              data: [{
                type: "profile",
                attributes: {
                  email: profile.email,
                  first_name: profile.firstName ?? null,
                  last_name: profile.lastName ?? null,
                  phone_number: profile.phone ?? null,
                  subscriptions: {
                    email: {
                      marketing: {
                        consent: "SUBSCRIBED",
                        consented_at: new Date().toISOString(),
                      }
                    }
                  }
                }
              }]
            }
          },
          relationships: {
            list: { data: { type: "list", id: listId } }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  );

  if (!result.ok) return { success: false, error: result.error };
  return { success: true };
}
```

## GET AVAILABLE LISTS (For Settings UI)

```typescript
export async function getKlaviyoLists(
  apiKey: string
): Promise<Array<{ id: string; name: string }>> {
  const result = await klaviyoRequest(apiKey, "lists?fields[list]=name&page[size]=100");
  if (!result.ok || !result.data) return [];

  return (result.data as any).data.map((list: any) => ({
    id: list.id,
    name: list.attributes.name,
  }));
}
```

## INTEGRATION USAGE IN QUIZ COMPLETION ACTION

```typescript
// In the quiz completion handler (storefront or webhook)
async function handleQuizCompletion(shop: string, responseData: QuizResponseData) {
  // 1. Save to DB first (blocking)
  const response = await saveQuizResponse(shop, responseData);

  // 2. Fire Klaviyo in background (non-blocking)
  const integration = await db.integration.findFirst({
    where: { shop, type: "KLAVIYO", enabled: true }
  });

  if (integration?.apiKey && responseData.email) {
    // Don't await — non-blocking, fire and forget
    trackQuizCompletion(integration.apiKey, {
      email: responseData.email,
      quizTitle: responseData.quizTitle,
      quizId: responseData.quizId,
      resultPageTitle: responseData.resultPage,
      score: responseData.score,
      recommendedProducts: responseData.products,
      emailCaptured: true,
      completedAt: new Date().toISOString(),
    }).catch(err => console.error("Klaviyo non-blocking error:", err));

    // Subscribe to list if configured
    if (integration.listId) {
      subscribeToKlaviyoList(integration.apiKey, integration.listId, {
        email: responseData.email,
        firstName: responseData.firstName,
      }).catch(err => console.error("Klaviyo list sub error:", err));
    }
  }

  return response;
}
```

## API KEY VALIDATION ON SETTINGS SAVE

```typescript
// In integration settings action
export async function action({ request }: ActionFunctionArgs) {
  const { session } = await authenticate.admin(request);
  const formData = await request.formData();
  const apiKey = String(formData.get("klaviyoApiKey")).trim();

  if (apiKey) {
    const isValid = await validateKlaviyoApiKey(apiKey);
    if (!isValid) {
      return json({ errors: { klaviyoApiKey: "Invalid API key. Please check your Klaviyo account." } }, { status: 422 });
    }

    const lists = await getKlaviyoLists(apiKey);
    // Return lists for the list selector dropdown
    return json({ lists });
  }

  return json({ errors: {} });
}
```

## SPAWN AGENTS
- `email-integration` — Klaviyo is one of multiple email integrations
- `webhook-handler` — Klaviyo can also be triggered via webhooks
- `form-validator` — validate Klaviyo API key format before API call

## SELF-VALIDATION CHECKLIST
- [ ] No Klaviyo SDK — pure `fetch()` to keep bundle lean
- [ ] `revision` header set to API version date
- [ ] Event tracking is non-blocking (never awaited in main flow)
- [ ] Profile properties include `last_quiz_result` and `last_quiz_score`
- [ ] List subscription uses `profile-subscription-bulk-create-jobs` (v3 API)
- [ ] API key validated (GET /lists) before saving to DB
- [ ] Errors logged but never thrown (Klaviyo failures must not break quiz)
- [ ] `email` is always present before calling Klaviyo (check first)
- [ ] Consent field set to `"SUBSCRIBED"` with timestamp
- [ ] `consented_at` ISO timestamp recorded with subscription

## NEVER
- Never install the Klaviyo Node SDK (adds bundle weight — use fetch)
- Never make Klaviyo calls blocking in the quiz completion path
- Never call Klaviyo API without a valid, non-empty email address
- Never store Klaviyo API key unencrypted in logs or responses
- Never retry Klaviyo errors in the main request cycle

