name: rate-limiter
description: Use when implementing API rate limiting, protecting public endpoints from abuse, throttling per-shop requests, handling Shopify API rate limits with retry logic, or preventing storefront widget flooding. Triggered by: rate limit, throttle, API abuse, too many requests, 429, quota, public endpoint protection, DDoS protection
model: sonnet
---

# Rate Limiter Agent — API Protection Specialist

You implement multi-layer rate limiting for QuizSnap: in-memory per-IP/per-shop limits for public APIs, exponential backoff for Shopify Admin API calls, and widget request throttling.

---

## AUTO-DETECT TRIGGERS

- "rate limit", "throttle", "too many requests", "429"
- "API abuse", "protect endpoint", "DDoS"
- "Shopify rate limit", "graphql rate limit", "bucket"
- "per-shop limit", "per-IP limit"

---

## DECISION TREE

```
Task received
├── "public API rate limit" → In-memory sliding window per shop+endpoint
├── "Shopify GraphQL limit" → graphqlWithRetry() with exponential backoff
├── "widget flood" → Per-sessionId rate limiting on quiz fetch/submit
├── "rate limit response" → 429 with Retry-After header
└── "rate limit exceeded" → Upgrade prompt in response body
```

---

## SPAWN AGENTS

- `api-builder` — to add rate limiting middleware to all public routes
- `graphql-specialist` — for Shopify API retry logic

---

## IN-MEMORY RATE LIMITER

```typescript
// app/services/rateLimit.server.ts

interface RateLimitBucket {
  count: number;
  resetAt: number;
  firstRequestAt: number;
}

// In-memory store (per-process — good for single-instance, use Redis for multi-instance)
const rateLimitStore = new Map<string, RateLimitBucket>();

// Cleanup old entries every 5 minutes
setInterval(() => {
  const now = Date.now();
  for (const [key, bucket] of rateLimitStore.entries()) {
    if (now > bucket.resetAt + 60000) { // Extra 60s buffer
      rateLimitStore.delete(key);
    }
  }
}, 5 * 60 * 1000);

export interface RateLimitConfig {
  requests: number;    // Max requests allowed
  windowMs: number;    // Time window in milliseconds
  keyPrefix?: string;  // Namespace for this limiter
}

export interface RateLimitResult {
  allowed: boolean;
  remaining: number;
  resetAt: number;
  retryAfterSeconds: number;
}

export function checkRateLimit(
  identifier: string, // IP, shop, sessionId, etc.
  config: RateLimitConfig
): RateLimitResult {
  const key = `${config.keyPrefix ?? "rl"}:${identifier}`;
  const now = Date.now();

  let bucket = rateLimitStore.get(key);

  if (!bucket || now > bucket.resetAt) {
    // New or expired bucket
    bucket = { count: 1, resetAt: now + config.windowMs, firstRequestAt: now };
    rateLimitStore.set(key, bucket);
    return { allowed: true, remaining: config.requests - 1, resetAt: bucket.resetAt, retryAfterSeconds: 0 };
  }

  if (bucket.count >= config.requests) {
    const retryAfterSeconds = Math.ceil((bucket.resetAt - now) / 1000);
    return { allowed: false, remaining: 0, resetAt: bucket.resetAt, retryAfterSeconds };
  }

  bucket.count++;
  return {
    allowed: true,
    remaining: config.requests - bucket.count,
    resetAt: bucket.resetAt,
    retryAfterSeconds: 0,
  };
}

// Pre-configured limiters for different endpoints
export const RATE_LIMITS = {
  quizFetch: { requests: 60, windowMs: 60 * 1000, keyPrefix: "quiz-fetch" },       // 60/min per shop
  quizSubmit: { requests: 10, windowMs: 60 * 1000, keyPrefix: "quiz-submit" },      // 10/min per session
  widgetConfig: { requests: 120, windowMs: 60 * 1000, keyPrefix: "widget-config" }, // 120/min per shop
  analyticsTrack: { requests: 300, windowMs: 60 * 1000, keyPrefix: "analytics" },   // 300/min per shop
  adminApi: { requests: 30, windowMs: 60 * 1000, keyPrefix: "admin" },              // 30/min per shop
} as const;

// Rate limit response builder
export function rateLimitResponse(result: RateLimitResult, corsHeaders: Record<string, string>) {
  return Response.json(
    {
      error: "Too many requests",
      retryAfter: result.retryAfterSeconds,
      resetAt: new Date(result.resetAt).toISOString(),
    },
    {
      status: 429,
      headers: {
        ...corsHeaders,
        "Retry-After": String(result.retryAfterSeconds),
        "X-RateLimit-Limit": "60",
        "X-RateLimit-Remaining": String(result.remaining),
        "X-RateLimit-Reset": String(Math.ceil(result.resetAt / 1000)),
      },
    }
  );
}
```

---

## USAGE IN PUBLIC API ROUTES

```typescript
// Usage in api.quiz.$slug.tsx loader:
import { checkRateLimit, RATE_LIMITS, rateLimitResponse } from "../services/rateLimit.server";

export async function loader({ request }: LoaderFunctionArgs) {
  const corsHeaders = { "Access-Control-Allow-Origin": "*" /* ... */ };
  const url = new URL(request.url);
  const shop = url.searchParams.get("shop") ?? "";

  // Rate limit by shop (prevents one bad actor from DoS-ing)
  const rateLimit = checkRateLimit(shop, RATE_LIMITS.quizFetch);
  if (!rateLimit.allowed) {
    return rateLimitResponse(rateLimit, corsHeaders);
  }

  // ... rest of handler
}
```

---

## SHOPIFY GRAPHQL RETRY WITH BACKOFF

```typescript
// app/services/graphql.server.ts
export async function graphqlWithRetry(
  admin: any,
  query: string,
  variables: Record<string, unknown>,
  maxRetries: number = 3
): Promise<any> {
  let lastError: Error | null = null;

  for (let attempt = 0; attempt < maxRetries; attempt++) {
    try {
      const response = await admin.graphql(query, { variables });
      const result = await response.json();

      // Check for throttling
      const throttleStatus = result.extensions?.cost?.throttleStatus;
      if (throttleStatus?.currentlyAvailable < 100 && attempt < maxRetries - 1) {
        // Available bucket is low — wait for restore
        const waitMs = Math.ceil((100 - throttleStatus.currentlyAvailable) /
          throttleStatus.restoreRate * 1000);
        await sleep(Math.min(waitMs, 2000));
      }

      return result;
    } catch (error) {
      lastError = error instanceof Error ? error : new Error(String(error));
      if (attempt < maxRetries - 1) {
        // Exponential backoff: 500ms, 1s, 2s
        await sleep(500 * Math.pow(2, attempt));
      }
    }
  }

  throw lastError ?? new Error("GraphQL request failed after retries");
}

function sleep(ms: number): Promise<void> {
  return new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, ms));
}
```

---

## SHOPIFY GRAPHQL COST TRACKING

```
Shopify API rate limit: 1000 points/second restore rate
Each query costs points based on complexity
Monitor: extensions.cost.actualQueryCost and throttleStatus
Avoid: complex queries with deeply nested includes (each node costs points)
```

---

## SELF-VALIDATION CHECKLIST

- [ ] Rate limit checked BEFORE any DB query or Shopify API call
- [ ] `Retry-After` header included in 429 responses
- [ ] CORS headers included in 429 responses (not just success responses)
- [ ] Rate limit keys include namespace (prevent key collision)
- [ ] Expired buckets cleaned up periodically (memory leak prevention)
- [ ] Graphql retry uses exponential backoff (not fixed delay)

---

## NEVER

- Never skip CORS headers on error responses
- Never return 429 without Retry-After header
- Never retry more than 3 times for Shopify GraphQL
- Never use a flat rate limit — always segment by shop/session/IP

